A||||7||Robert||You want to see some Fiero’s … Just drive your truck||||10||
Z||000000||Robert||08-03-2000||10:58 AM||||Yesterday I was on my way to Home Depot to get some fence lumber, so I was in my trusty old Toyota pickup.  Home Depot (They always greet me with a “Hi Robert, back again”?) is just two exits down the freeway from me, so as I am exiting the freeway I noticed a black SE waiting at the light.  After leaving Home Depot, I see a gold SE within a couple of blocks.  Getting off the freeway, a red GT passes me on the right.  Two blocks from my house a silver GT is parked in the driveway, (I see this one about every three weeks, must be visiting family).   As usual there is the trashed white 2m4 in the driveway of one of my neighbors houses, (I’ve tried to get this lady to fix up here car, but she just doesn’t care). <P>Isn’t it ironic that I always see other Fiero’s whenever I’m driving something else?  I could drive my Fiero for week and not see another Fiero.<P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||b lo 0||08-03-2000||11:06 AM||||It's not just you.  The same thing happens in my Jeep Wrangler.  When I'm in it, I never EVER see another open-body Jeep.  When I'm in the Fiero I'm SURROUNDED by Jeeps.  Funny how that happens.  I never see Fiero's though, except for the occasional 2M4 (I'm convinced I'm the only one in Gwinnett County with a V6, let alone a GT.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||08-03-2000||11:22 AM||||happened just this week. i always see fieros but with the show just here i saw customised ones while i was in my truck or out running. i waved but i guess i just someone looking at a fixed up car. one had ky. plates though. wonder where they're from. black gt, with a raised rear wing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||08-03-2000||12:29 PM||||Too true. While my car has been in the shop undergoing its engine swap a cute brunette across the street has moved in with a black fastback GT. I talked to her briefly one morning and complimented her on her car, but I wish I would have had my GT there too to show her. Damn!||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||08-03-2000||01:12 PM||||Of course you see more Fieros when you're driving another vehicle!  All (well, most)   other vehicles are higher - so you see more of everything.<P>When I switch from driving one of the Fieros to my Cavalier, I feel like I'm driving a truck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !  ||||reg||12
Z||000005||tgowens||08-03-2000||01:17 PM||||Robert, that was another poker run -- they all saw three marks on the curb!! aren't you glad you were going the other way?? -- I need to get back there so I can see some Fieros -- they are non-existent here!!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||08-03-2000||09:34 PM||||Thats one of the reasons why I love Fieros so much..because you rarely see them. Mustangs, Camaros, Civics, Jeeps, and even Vettes....dime a dozen. Everywhere I look I see these cars. My roommate has a 98 Mustang Gt convertible...silver w/ the black "styling bar" (roll bar looking thing), and silver Integral SSR wheels (5 spoke, 18"..nice). Its a beautiful car, and hes proud of it..as he should be. But, all I have to do is go outside and Im literally tripping over Mustangs....theyre EVERYWHERE!<BR>Thats why I love the uniqueness (sp?) of Fieros...you rarely see them, and I ALWAYS get looks, thumbs up, and great comments about them!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>p.s. no offense intended to anyone who owns the affore mentioned cars (minus the Fiero of course)..they are all nice cars, I was just making a point!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||HYPTNOTiSE||08-04-2000||09:21 AM||||I agree! I see a nice fiero and i honk my horn and wave and act all crazy, and then i look down and i'm in my 89 s-10 and they probably think i'm insane.  Ah well. "Time to go back to your room now Mike."<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
